WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
Squeeze a cold pack, and
within seconds it feels icy.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.290
Inside, a solid is dissolving in water.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.370
Your hand feels the cold.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.010
But what is happening to the
energy of the chemicals themselves?

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:18.510
When a cold pack goes cold, has the
chemical inside lost energy, or gained it?

6
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.670
In this mission, you'll separate
a system from its surroundings,

7
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.230
and see why heat is not
the same as temperature.

8
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.550
You'll tell exothermic from endothermic,

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.650
and read energy profiles,
activation energy and all.

10
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.520
Your mission: work out where the
energy goes when a cold pack goes cold.
